Author: HaoVX <166486883+SzeHaoVX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 10 11:56:50 2026 +0800

    Add word-by-word text reveal synced to narration in Azr_Explain
    
    The explanation widget can now clear its sentence when the learner presses
    Play and rebuild it a word at a time in step with the voice-over. Off by
    default, so existing content keeps the static sentence.
    
    Two paths. Fill in a step's Word Timings and the reveal is driven straight
    off those numbers and matches the narration exactly. Leave it blank and the
    reveal estimates the pacing from the audio's own loudness envelope, which
    follows the voice but drifts - measured at up to 0.97s by mid-sentence,
    worst across the pauses between paragraphs.
    
    Timings are per language because each language is a separate recording with
    its own word count, and are rejected rather than trusted when the count
    disagrees with the sentence on screen; a stale list would desynchronise
    confidently instead of failing safe.
    
    The audio component is now built explicitly rather than through
    SpawnSoundAttached, because the envelope feed is decided when a sound starts
    and SpawnSoundAttached starts it on creation, a frame too late to bind. That
    also fixes a latent bug where every step of an Explain+ chain played from the
    first step's widget location.
    
    Tools/Azr-ElevenLabsTimings.ps1 generates the narration and the matching word
    timings from ElevenLabs in one call, walking down the output-format ladder to
    whatever the account's tier allows. It carries a -SelfTest that exercises the
    timing maths with no API call.

